From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 22:36:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] net: phy: as21xxx: tighten firmware bootstrap path

Reject empty or odd-sized runtime firmware images and propagate errors from the indirect-loader status read.

Based on the tested local migration by Guangda Ji in commit ceab4fe4af329eb191d54598feffa4af2e4abf93. Adapted to Linux 6.18 after the current OpenWrt AS21xxx fixes.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c b/drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c
index c65f4a8..f30a41e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c
@@ -300,6 +300,11 @@ static int aeon_firmware_boot(struct phy_device *phydev, const u8 *data,
 	int i, ret;
 	u16 val;
 
+	if (!size || size % sizeof(u16)) {
+		phydev_err(phydev, "invalid firmware size: %zu\n", size);
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
 	ret = phy_modify_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND1, VEND1_GLB_REG_CPU_CTRL,
 			     VEND1_GLB_CPU_CTRL_MASK, AEON_CPU_CTRL_FW_LOAD);
 	if (ret)
@@ -316,8 +321,12 @@ static int aeon_firmware_boot(struct phy_device *phydev, const u8 *data,
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	val = phy_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND1,
+	ret = phy_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND1,
 			   VEND1_GLB_REG_MDIO_INDIRECT_STATUS);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+
+	val = ret;
 	if (val > 1) {
 		phydev_err(phydev, "wrong origin mdio_indirect_status: %x\n", val);
 		return -EINVAL;
